<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<!-- $title = ROAD TRAIN DOMAIN.txt -->
<!-- $desc = A campaign built around three simple rules for safely sharing the road with road trains. The idea was to establish regional WA as a different driving environment, where understanding these rules is essential. -->
<!-- @import '../head.kit' -->

<body class="">
    <!-- @import '../header.kit' -->
    <div class="main">
        <div class="project-intro typewriter">
            <div class="project-intro-inner">
                <h1 class="project-title" data-chars="1" data-speed="50">Welcome to the Road Train Domain</h1>
                <hr>
                <div class="project-details-wrapper">
                    <div class="project-details">
                        <h2>Client</h2>
                        <p>Main Roads WA</p>

                        <h2>Involvement</h2>
                        <p>Storyboarding</p>
                        <p>Animation</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="project-description">
                        <h2>Challenge</h2>
                        <p>Driving outside Perth comes with a different set of challenges. Regional WA is full of long, open roads and road trains, which are essential to keeping the state moving. But for drivers unfamiliar with country roads, knowing how to safely share the road with these trucks can be tricky. Main Roads WA needed a campaign to educate city drivers on the basics of country driving and help keep everyone safe.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="project-description">
                        <h2>Solution</h2>
                        
                        <p>Together with Block, we created the Road Train Domain, a campaign built around three simple rules for safely sharing the road with road trains. The idea was to establish regional WA as a different driving environment, where understanding these rules is essential. We brought the campaign to life through out-of-home advertising and radio across regional WA, reaching drivers where they were most likely to need the information.</p>
                        <p>Under Block's direction, I storyboarded and animated the feature ad for the campaign and helped create the key assets for the rest of the&nbsp;rollout.</p>
                        <div class="collab-logos wait-for-typewriter">
                            <img alt="Cameron Murray" title="Cameron Murray" src="/assets/logo-cameron-murray.svg">
                            <img alt="Block Branding" title="Block Branding" src="/assets/logo-block.svg">
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="project-content">
            <div class="video-embed-wrapper"><iframe src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1120710907?autopause=0&amp;player_id=0&amp;app_id=58479" frameborder="0" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" style="position:absolute;top:0;left:0;width:100%;height:100%;" title="Road Train Domain"></iframe></div><script src="https://player.vimeo.com/api/player.js"></script>

            <div class="expandable"><img src="images/road-train-domain-1.webp"></div>
            <div class="expandable"><img src="images/road-train-domain-2.webp"></div>
            <div class="expandable">
                <video autoplay loop muted playsinline>
                  <source src="images/road-train-domain-video-1.webm" type="video/webm">
                  Your browser does not support the video tag.
                </video>
            </div>
            <div class="expandable"><img src="images/road-train-domain-3.webp"></div>
            <div class="expandable"><img src="images/road-train-domain-6.webp"></div>
            

        </div>
    </div>
    <!-- @import '../footer.kit' -->
</body>

</html>